Package: TruncComp
Type: Package
Title: Two-Component Comparisons for Outcomes with a Substantive Atom
Version: 0.2.0
Author: Andreas Kryger Jensen
Maintainer: Andreas Kryger Jensen <aeje@sund.ku.dk>
Description: Implements parametric and semiparametric likelihood ratio methods
    for comparing two groups when a continuous outcome may be undefined because
    a substantive event has occurred. The methods jointly assess treatment
    contrasts in the conditional non-atom mean and the probability outside the
    atom. The package also provides
    component intervals, joint component regions, coded-endpoint intervals for
    unadjusted analyses, and an experimental Bayesian two-part mixture model.
